"""src/error — the SipiError exception base and the SipiValueError value type.

`metadata`, `format_handlers`, and `iiifparser` all throw/catch `SipiError` without
depending on the image engine; folding the type into `//src/image` would
close an `image -> metadata -> image` cycle Bazel cannot express. This
package is the tree's foundational leaf: everything above it (`metadata`,
`format_handlers`, `iiifparser`, the image engine) depends on it, and it depends on
nothing above itself.

`SipiValueError` (ADR-0024) is the image/codec layer's value-returning
replacement for `SipiImageError`; it lives here rather than in `//src/image`
for the same reason `SipiError` does — every consumer of the image/codec
layer already depends on this package without a cycle. It is header-only:
no eager formatting happens at construction, so there is nothing to put in a
translation unit.

`include_prefix = "error"` + `strip_include_prefix = "/src/error/cpp"`
exposes the headers at `#include "error/SipiError.h"` / `#include
"error/SipiValueError.h"` for cross-package consumers; siblings inside this
package use the bare quote form (`#include "SipiError.h"`).
"""

load("@rules_cc//cc:defs.bzl", "cc_library", "cc_test")

package(default_visibility = ["//src:__subpackages__"])

cc_library(
    name = "error",
    srcs = ["cpp/SipiError.cpp"],
    hdrs = [
        "cpp/SipiError.h",
        "cpp/SipiValueError.h",
    ],
    include_prefix = "error",
    strip_include_prefix = "/src/error/cpp",
    deps = [
        "//src/util",
    ],
)

# Colocated unit test (ADR-0003) for the header-only SipiValueError value
# type: ErrorCode/policy_for completeness and the client_message()/
# diagnostic_message() behavior it must reproduce from SipiImageError.
cc_test(
    name = "error_test",
    srcs = ["cpp/sipi_value_error_test.cpp"],
    deps = [
        ":error",
        "@googletest//:gtest_main",
    ],
)
